# The variables the server's .env must give, non-empty, for the application to start (DEPLOY.md, "首次部署前" step 2):
# a name per line, optionally followed by the shortest value the application accepts (`-` for any) and by how the
# value must start; a name marked `?` may be absent, but when given is checked the same. The deploy workflow checks the
# .env against this list before it pulls the image: a missing variable stops the deployment before Flyway migrates the
# database, which an older release could not run on afterwards (DEPLOY.md, "从 1.2 切到 1.3"). The list goes with each
# commit, so that a rollback is checked against the variables of its own release.

# Database (create-db.sh's output)
SPRING_R2DBC_URL
SPRING_R2DBC_USERNAME
SPRING_R2DBC_PASSWORD
SPRING_FLYWAY_URL
SPRING_FLYWAY_USER
SPRING_FLYWAY_PASSWORD

# Platform keys: Base64 of at least 32 bytes (the application checks their length)
JABIZ_JWT_SECRET
JABIZ_INTEGRITY_KEY
JABIZ_MFA_KEY
JABIZ_SEAL_KEY

# Stripe (Q6a, Q6b)
STRIPE_API_KEY
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET
STRIPE_CONNECT_WEBHOOK_SECRET

# Claude (Q8a)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY

# QuizBuks for Shopify (S1): placeholders until the Shopify app exists; the secret of at least 32 characters
SHOPIFY_API_KEY
SHOPIFY_API_SECRET 32

# Signing in with providers: needed only with the Spring profile that declares them (`<profile>:NAME`; Q40, platform
# 17j). "google" has Google's client; "social" Google's, Apple's, Facebook's and LINE's (LINE's secret of at least 32
# bytes, Apple's key a .p8 file), all with the callbacks of the app and the sponsor console.
google:JABIZ_OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
google:JABIZ_OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
google:QB_OIDC_REDIRECT_APP - https://
google:QB_OIDC_REDIRECT_SPONSOR - https://
social:JABIZ_OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
social:JABIZ_OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
social:JABIZ_OIDC_APPLE_CLIENT_ID
social:JABIZ_OIDC_APPLE_TEAM_ID 10
social:JABIZ_OIDC_APPLE_KEY_ID 10
social:JABIZ_OIDC_APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY
social:QB_OIDC_APPLE_FORM_POST - https://
social:JABIZ_OIDC_FACEBOOK_CLIENT_ID
social:JABIZ_OIDC_FACEBOOK_CLIENT_SECRET
social:JABIZ_OIDC_LINE_CLIENT_ID
social:JABIZ_OIDC_LINE_CLIENT_SECRET 32
social:QB_OIDC_REDIRECT_APP - https://
social:QB_OIDC_REDIRECT_SPONSOR - https://

# Account deletion's maintenance connection (platform 17i, DEPLOY.md "1a"): optional; when given, the R2DBC URL, not
# the JDBC one Flyway takes (the application refuses to start with it)
?JABIZ_ERASURE_DATASOURCE_URL - r2dbc:

# Push notifications (platform 17k): with the Spring profile "push", the VAPID key pair (Base64url: the public key 87
# characters, the private key 43) and the push services' contact (a mailto: address)
push:JABIZ_PUSH_PUBLIC_KEY 87
push:JABIZ_PUSH_PRIVATE_KEY 43
push:JABIZ_PUSH_SUBJECT - mailto:
